# GoShiSen-Enforce — SSH allowed signers for release tags.
#
# Tag signing is a GOAL, not an active requirement: once the maintainer
# configures a signing key and replaces the placeholder below with the
# real public key, the release tag (vX.Y.Z) must be signed with an SSH
# key listed here; scripts/release-pin-gate.sh then enforces it
# (GATE_TAG_SIGN_CHECK=1) and users verify with:  git tag -v vX.Y.Z
# Until the placeholder is replaced, tags are annotated but unsigned and
# the signature check is not an active requirement.
#
# Format (one key per line):  <principal> ssh-ed25519 <base64-pubkey>
# Replace the placeholder below with the maintainer's release key.
# See docs/release/signed-tags-plan.md for the full procedure.
#
# maintainer@example.com ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
